'' A WIDE value appended to a NARROW var-length string -- a DWSTRING-shaped UDT, a plain wstring,
'' a wstring deref, 'wstr( )', an rvalue UDT, a rendered number beside it, '+=', a value that
'' reads the destination, and tracks' 's &= "host=" & this.Host & "|"' in a method. Every one
'' was DROPPED (one more statement not lowered) because narrow EmitStrTerm has no form for a
'' wide term; 'h &= u & wz', with a ustring in the chain, lowered and held "nU w i". Measured,
'' fbc-modern prints the lines listed in the source's header; tiko prints the same lines now.
''
'' The dual-cast UDT stays NARROW, as fbc has it. One deliberate difference: fbc builds the DS
'' chains through the user 'operator &' overloads, tiko through fb_WstrConcatAW -- the same text,
'' since the destination is narrow either way, and no operator temporaries.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/narrow-append-wide.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: call ptr _ZN2DScvwEv(@d)
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_WstrConcatAW(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_WstrAssignToA(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_UStrConcatAU(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_UStrAssignToA(
'' EXPECT-OUT: call ptr _ZN4DUALcv8FBSTRINGEv(@du)
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_StrConcatAssign(
'' EXPECT-NOT: call ptr _Zv23cat
'' EXPECT-NOT: call ptr _ZN4DUALcvwEv
